From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:07:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 001/342] efi/arm64: accept PSCI 0.2 firmware, not only
 "arm,psci-1.0"

The device tree PSCI node was only recognised when its first compatible
string was "arm,psci-1.0". Firmware that implements PSCI 0.2, like the
Amlogic S905 BL31 on the ODROID-C2 ("arm,psci-0.2"), left sPsciCallFn
NULL while the CPU nodes still asked for enable-method "psci", so starting
the secondary CPUs called through a NULL pointer after ExitBootServices.

Match "arm,psci-1.0", "arm,psci-0.2" or "arm,psci" anywhere in the list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_dtb.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/system/boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_dtb.cpp b/src/system/boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_dtb.cpp
index b0257341bb..8526d88a03 100644
--- a/src/system/boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_dtb.cpp
+++ b/src/system/boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_dtb.cpp
@@ -70,8 +70,13 @@ arch_handle_fdt(const void* fdt, int node)
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (strcmp(compatible, "arm,psci-1.0") == 0)
+	// Firmware lists the PSCI versions it implements, newest first; the
+	// Amlogic S905 (ODROID-C2) BL31 only claims "arm,psci-0.2".
+	if (dtb_has_fdt_string(compatible, compatibleLen, "arm,psci-1.0")
+		|| dtb_has_fdt_string(compatible, compatibleLen, "arm,psci-0.2")
+		|| dtb_has_fdt_string(compatible, compatibleLen, "arm,psci")) {
 		arm64_handle_fdt_psci_node(fdt, node);
+	}
 }
 
 
